# THE GS-QUANT PARITY OF #TS (tools/gs-quant-oracle/README.md, 2026-11-07): every case of the oracle's mapping -- a
# word of the library as a #TS item -- run on DuckDB and judged against gs-quant's own function at the oracle's pin
# (tools/gs-quant-oracle/pins.env), snapped by tools/gs-quant-oracle/snap.py (1e-9 absolute, 1e-8 relative for a
# volatility, a correlation, a beta), over three datasets: the gallery's samples and the adversarial fixture's two price
# files, raw and adjusted, each its own answers and ledger. Each case's verdict is held by its ledger, a DIFF written
# with lite's SQL to the undeclared outputs (gsquant-findings.md); JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS=-Dts.gsquant.update=<the oracle's
# directory in the workspace> rewrites the ledgers' verdicts (the JUnit launcher takes no -D).
