junit_test(
    name = "cypher_parity_test",
    # eternal (3600 s), the size kept (2026-10-19): main's Windows core lane timed it out at large's 900 s three times on
    # 167018c4 (runs 39164681359 and 39262226227); measured 451-820 s on Linux and macOS and 645 s on Windows when
    # green. Eight temporal cases send 0.3-34 MB of SQL each (CypherToPure's temporal helpers repeat an input in every
    # use: lite/temporal/nanos_arithmetic is one 33.7 MB statement, 130 s in DuckDB's prepare) and take 75% of the
    # lane (throwaway branch debug/cypher-parity-timing). Back to large's own timeout when the translator binds a
